# Title: Potential Credential Dumping Activity Via LSASS
# ID: 5ef9853e-4d0e-4a70-846f-a9ca37d876da
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: Samir Bousseaden, Michael Haag
# Date: 2019-04-03
# Tags: attack.credential-access, attack.t1003.001, attack.s0002
# Description: Detects process access requests to the LSASS process with specific call trace calls and access masks.
# This behaviour is expressed by many credential dumping tools such as Mimikatz, NanoDump, Invoke-Mimikatz, Procdump and even the Taskmgr dumping feature.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((TargetImage="*\\lsass.exe" AND (GrantedAccess CONTAIN "0x1038" OR GrantedAccess CONTAIN "0x1438" OR GrantedAccess CONTAIN "0x143a" OR GrantedAccess CONTAIN "0x1fffff") AND (CallTrace CONTAIN "dbgcore.dll" OR CallTrace CONTAIN "dbghelp.dll" OR CallTrace CONTAIN "kernel32.dll" OR CallTrace CONTAIN "kernelbase.dll" OR CallTrace CONTAIN "ntdll.dll")) AND NOT (((SourceUser CONTAIN "AUTHORI" OR SourceUser CONTAIN "AUTORI"))) AND NOT ((((SourceImage="*:\\Windows\\Sysmon64.exe" OR SourceImage="*:\\Windows\\Sysmon64a.exe")) OR ((CallTrace CONTAIN ":\\Windows\\Temp\\asgard2-agent\\" AND CallTrace CONTAIN "\\thor\\thor64.exe+" AND CallTrace CONTAIN "|UNKNOWN(") AND GrantedAccess = "0x103800"))))
